% referencias.bib: bibliography of the PIBIC-ITA final report (DUNE-GNN), October 2026.
% Built on 2026-10-14 from research/refs_physics.bib and research/refs_ml.bib, plus Efron (1979).
% Provenance and verification of every entry: research/physics_background.md (section 10),
% research/literature_ml.md (section 18) and research/bibliography_report.md (changes made here).
% Style: abntex2cite [alf] with abntex2-alf.bst. The style prints the titles of articles, papers
% and chapters in sentence case, so proper nouns and acronyms in those titles stay in braces,
% and the first letter after a colon is written in lower case because BibTeX keeps a capital
% there; titles of books, reports and preprints print as written and are given in sentence case.
% DOIs print through url (https://doi.org/...) followed by urlaccessdate; the doi, eprint and
% archiveprefix fields are kept for other tools and are ignored by abntex2.
% The access date is written with ties, 14~out.~2026, so that it never breaks across lines.
% Series are written as a closing note, (Series, v. n), so that they print after the pages.
% Issue numbers are written without leading zeros (8, not the 08 of the JINST metadata); DOIs and
% URLs keep the zeros. Collaboration papers carry no collaboration note; the note "Em nome da
% Colaboracao" marks only a single author writing on behalf of a collaboration.
% Four or more authors print as the first author followed by et al. (abntex2 default list option).
% Only cited keys appear in the PDF. Never use \nocite{*} with abntex2cite: it also pulls in
% the option entries of abntex2-options.bib and breaks the bibliography.

